WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:21.250
<v Pledgivo>A campaign, a gift, and your own website

2
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:40.370
<v 1. The campaign>Three lookups do all the work — Designation, payment account and design decide everything downstream

3
00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:55.370
<v 2. The donor's path>The page a donor actually gets — Story on the left, the whole gift on the right - no page changes

4
00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:15.190
<v 2. The donor's path>Card details, and only card details — The Stripe element is the one place a card number is ever typed

5
00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:42.890
<v 2. The donor's path>Confirmed - but not yet recorded — Salesforce writes the donation later, from a scheduled job

6
00:01:42.890 --> 00:02:03.310
<v 3. On your own website>Copy the snippet — A script tag plus one div; the mode toggle rewrites both

7
00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:24.780
<v 3. On your own website>Running on a site that is not Salesforce — Card, button and form - carrying the campaign's own colours across

8
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:50.150
<v 3. On your own website>The handoff — Amount, name and email arrive on the donation page already filled in

9
00:02:50.150 --> 00:03:11.750
<v Wrap up>One campaign, live in two places.

10
00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:38.680
<v About Pledgivo>Fundraising and donation management, native to Salesforce. Docs: pledgivo.cloudalgo.com

